     1	"""Derived, substitution-only ASO sites in GRCh38 / GENCODE v50 pre-mRNA.
     2	
     3	Coverage: complete contiguous gene bodies, including exons AND introns, on the
     4	annotated gene strand; no intergenic sequence, no exon-union index, and no
     5	splice-concatenated RNA. A hit must fit entirely inside its gene. Ambiguous
     6	reference bases count as substitutions, never wildcards. K defaults to 3 (use
     7	0, 1, 2, or 3 for the usual nested universes); edit distance is not implemented.
     8	
     9	The GTF loader reads gene records only. Consequently region_class and transcript
    10	membership are not_available/null unless callers supply Transcript annotations.
    11	With annotations, junction-spanning means a *genomic exon/intron boundary*, not
    12	a spliced exon/exon junction. Alternative-transcript classes are preserved.
    13	Same ASO/coordinates/strand within one gene collapse to one record, with sorted
    14	transcript IDs; different genes (including paralogs) NEVER collapse. Gene-only
    15	records have transcript_ids=None, not a fabricated empty transcript list.
    16	
    17	Shards own genomic leftmost starts in closed, fixed chromosome windows; a right
    18	halo retains boundary hits on both strands. Region bounds restrict starts, not
    19	ends. IDs depend on coordinates/gene/ASO/sequence, not sharding or K. SMN ambiguity
    20	means the identical transcript-sense sequence was verified in the other SMN gene
    21	in the supplied gene universe, even if it lies outside the current shard.
    22	
    23	Outputs are explicit-schema Parquet, then an atomic .done JSON commit marker.
    24	Restart verifies parameters, input identities, row count, and Parquet SHA256.
    25	Input identities use resolved path/size/mtime_ns/inode plus FAI SHA256; they are
    26	filesystem identities, NOT full FASTA/GTF content hashes. Inputs must be immutable
    27	during a run. No full reference hashing or unbounded reference fetch is performed.
