+++ b/conference/model_v2/ops/briefs/J6_REVIEW_RESULT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+Verdict: **DO-NOT-ADVANCE** — 2 HIGH, 3 MED. Reviewed current working-tree files against SCIENTIFIC_LOCK.md and J6.md; no source edits.
+Paths below are relative to `conference/model_v2/`.
+
+- HIGH — `j6_site_universe.py:532`: FASTA identity records provenance but never verifies assembly; supplying a GRCh37 FASTA with the v50 GTF for an in-bounds chr5 region silently searches wrong coordinates and stamps results GRCh38. Fix: require a trusted GRCh38 reference manifest/signature before production enumeration; isolate synthetic-reference mode and add a mismatched-assembly rejection test.
+- HIGH — `j6_site_universe.py:399` / `j6_site_universe.py:540`: output-directory generations are not fenced; rerunning with another window size/region leaves obsolete, individually valid `.done` shards available for double counting or including out-of-universe sites. Tiny reproduction: window 4 then 6 on 12 A bases yields 5 committed files, 18 rows, only 9 unique sites. Fix: immutable run configuration plus an atomic manifest listing the exact expected/current shards, or reject incompatible directory reuse; test changed-window and changed-region restarts.
+- MED — `j6_site_universe.py:315` / `j6_site_universe.py:534`: region-filtered genes exclude the other SMN paralog, so an unchecked ambiguity becomes false. Reproduced: identical SMN1/SMN2 targets give true with both genes, false for the same site ID with SMN1 alone. Fix: retain both paralogs for ambiguity checks independently of output-region filtering, or represent unverified ambiguity as null/not_available; add a single-paralog-region test.
+- MED — `j6_site_universe.py:405`: every shard recursively serializes/hashes the entire gene universe; `:393` and `:274` also sort all genes per shard and `:285` scans them all. Full-genome work therefore incurs O(windows × genes) metadata processing even for empty outputs; unsharded `:281` additionally retains all output sites, contradicting the memory-bound claim at :270. Fix: cache immutable universe/hash and chromosome interval lookup once per worker, and expose streamed unsharded output; verify scaling with bounded synthetic data before production.
+- MED — `j6_site_universe.py:413` / `tests/test_j6_site_universe.py:182`: a `.done` containing valid JSON `[]` or `null` raises uncaught AttributeError on `manifest.get`, preventing restart recovery; both reproduced. Fix: validate manifest object/schema before access and rebuild invalid markers; extend corruption tests beyond malformed JSON.
+
+Requested command: `PYTHONPATH=feng/src /home/dashii/orcd/pool/smt-isef-env/bin/python -m pytest conference/model_v2/tests/test_j6_site_universe.py -q`.
+Exact requested-run counts: **42 passed, 0 skipped, 1 failed** (CLI subprocess SIGINT); isolated CLI-test retry: 0 passed, 0 skipped, 1 failed (same signal).
